  "question": {
    "text": "A steel wire of length 2 m and Young's modulus $2.0 \\times 10^{11} \\mathrm{Nm}^{-2}$ is stretched by a force. If Poisson ratio and transverse strain for the wire are 0.2 and $10^{-3}$ respectively, then the elastic potential energy density of the wire is _______ $\\times 10^5$ (in SI units)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "25",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\ell=2 \\mathrm{~m} ; \\mathrm{Y}=2 \\times 10^{11} \\frac{\\mathrm{~N}}{\\mathrm{~m}^2} \\\\ & \\begin{aligned} \\mu=-\\frac{\\left(\\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{r}}{\\mathrm{r}}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{\\Delta \\ell}{\\ell}\\right)} \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\Delta \\ell}{\\ell} & =\\frac{1}{\\mu} \\times\\left(\\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{r}}{\\mathrm{r}}\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{0.2} \\times\\left(10^{-3}\\right)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}$<br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\Delta \\ell}{\\ell}=5 \\times 10^{-3} \\\\ & \\begin{aligned} \\mathrm{u}=\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{y} \\varepsilon_{\\ell}^2 & =\\frac{1}{2} \\times 2 \\times 10^{11} \\times\\left[5 \\times 10^{-3}\\right]^2 \\\\ & =25\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
